  "content": {
    "id": "p69-q21-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p69-q21-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A company finds that it can sell ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " items per week at a price of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "p(x)=50-0.5x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " dollars per item. The fixed costs are $300, and each item costs $10 to produce.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p69-q21-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the revenue function $R(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R(x)=50x-\\frac{1}{2}x^2$ dollars.",
          "worked": "Revenue is quantity multiplied by price.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}R(x)&=x\\left(50-\\frac{1}{2}x\\right)\\\\R(x)&=50x-\\frac{1}{2}x^2\\quad\\text{dollars}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q21-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the cost function $C(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$C(x)=300+10x$ dollars.",
          "worked": "Cost is fixed cost plus variable cost.\n\n$$C(x)=300+10x\\quad\\text{dollars}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q21-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the profit function $P(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}x^2+40x-300$ dollars.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=R(x)-C(x)\\\\P(x)&=50x-\\frac{1}{2}x^2-(300+10x)\\\\P(x)&=-\\frac{1}{2}x^2+40x-300\\quad\\text{dollars}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q21-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "How many items should be sold to maximise the profit? What is the maximum profit?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p69-q21-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "40 items per week; maximum profit $500.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q21-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the vertex of the concave-down profit quadratic.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The coefficient of $x^2$ is negative, so the profit parabola has a maximum at its vertex. Its axis of symmetry is\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=-\\frac{40}{2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}\\\\x&=40.\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(40)&=-\\frac{1}{2}(40)^2+40(40)-300\\\\P(40)&=500.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe count must be a nonnegative integer. Here $40$ is an integer, and\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p(40)&=50-\\frac{1}{2}(40)\\\\p(40)&=30.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe selling price is positive, so the vertex gives a feasible item count and no rounding is needed. Sell 40 items per week for a maximum profit of $\\$500$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
